Store the awesome catalogue as JSON and draw it in one page.

Thirty generated pages carried the same 33k tool cards, so the data now lives
in docs/awesome/data/ — one index of categories, lists and drawers, plus one
file per shelf — and docs/awesomeIndex.html draws four collapsible levels from
it, fetching a shelf only when the reader opens it. Every href is emitted once:
the dataset keeps a shared seen set, so a tool in two shelves arrives as one
card that names the other list instead of a second link.

20 KB of page instead of 8.3 MB of HTML, and a shelf can be corrected by
editing its JSON rather than rebuilding a page.

